{"id":"mahabharata-13-005","work":"mahabharata","part":13,"partName":"अनुशासनपर्व","partNameEn":"Anushasana Parva","unit":5,"title":"पञ्चमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 5 · The parrot and the tree","summary":{"en":"Yudhishthira asks for the merits of kindness and of faithful devotees. Bhishma tells how Indra, in the form of a brahmin, tested an old parrot who would not leave his withered tree, which had given him shelter, and was pleased by the parrot's devotion.","kn":"ದಯೆ ಮತ್ತು ಭಕ್ತರ ಗುಣಗಳನ್ನು ಕೇಳಲು ಯುಧಿಷ್ಠಿರ ಬಯಸುತ್ತಾನೆ; ಇಂದ್ರ ಬ್ರಾಹ್ಮಣ ರೂಪದಲ್ಲಿ ಆಶ್ರಯ ನೀಡಿದ್ದ ಒಣಗಿದ ಮರವನ್ನು ಬಿಡದ ಮುದಿ ಗಿಳಿಯನ್ನು ಪರೀಕ್ಷಿಸಿ ಅದರ ಭಕ್ತಿಗೆ ಮೆಚ್ಚಿದ ಕಥೆಯನ್ನು ಭೀಷ್ಮ ಹೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"युधिष्ठिर दया और निष्ठावान भक्तों के गुण सुनना चाहते हैं, और भीष्म बताते हैं कि ब्राह्मण रूप में इन्द्र ने आश्रय देने वाले सूखे वृक्ष को न छोड़ने वाले बूढ़े तोते की परीक्षा ली और उसकी भक्ति से प्रसन्न हुए।","te":"దయ, నిష్ఠగల భక్తుల గుణాలను వినాలని యుధిష్ఠిరుడు కోరతాడు; బ్రాహ్మణ రూపంలో ఇంద్రుడు ఆశ్రయమిచ్చిన ఎండిన చెట్టును విడవని ముసలి చిలుకను పరీక్షించి దాని భక్తికి మెచ్చిన కథను భీష్ముడు చెబుతాడు.","ta":"கருணையின் பயனையும் பக்தர்களின் இயல்பையும் யுதிஷ்டிரர் கேட்க, அந்தண வடிவில் இந்திரன் தனக்கு அடைக்கலம் தந்த பட்ட மரத்தை விடாத முதிய கிளியைச் சோதித்து அதன் பக்தியில் மகிழ்ந்த கதையைப் பீஷ்மர் கூறுகிறார்.","ml":"ദയയുടെയും വിശ്വസ്തഭക്തരുടെയും പുണ്യമെന്തെന്ന് യുധിഷ്ഠിരൻ ചോദിക്കുന്നു. ബ്രാഹ്മണവേഷത്തിൽ ഇന്ദ്രൻ ഒരു വൃദ്ധനായ തത്തയെ പരീക്ഷിക്കുന്നു; ആശ്രയം നൽകിയ ഉണങ്ങിയ മരം വിട്ടുപോകാൻ അത് വിസമ്മതിക്കുന്നു. തത്തയുടെ ഭക്തിയിൽ ഇന്ദ്രൻ സന്തുഷ്ടനാകുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 13.5; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Tue Nov 03 2026","sections":[{"title":"आनुशासनिकपर्व","titleEn":"Anushasanika Parva (The instructions)","verses":[{"text":"युधिष्ठिर उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"आनृशंसस्य धर्मस्य गुणान्भक्तजनस्य च ।\nश्रोतुमिच्छामि कार्त्स्न्येन तन्मे ब्रूहि पितामह ॥","meaning":{"en":"Grandfather, I wish to hear in full about the virtues of the dharma of compassion and of a devoted person; tell me that."}},{"text":"भीष्म उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Bhishma said:"}},{"n":2,"text":"विषये काशिराजस्य ग्रामान्निष्क्रम्य लुब्धकः ।\nसविषं काण्डमादाय मृगयामास वै मृगम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"In the realm of the king of Kashi, a hunter left his village and went hunting for deer, taking a poisoned arrow."}},{"n":3,"text":"तत्र चामिषलुब्धेन लुब्धकेन महावने ।\nअविदूरे मृगं दृष्ट्वा बाणः प्रतिसमाहितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"In a great forest, that hunter, greedy for meat, saw a deer not far off and set an arrow to his bow."}},{"n":4,"text":"तेन दुर्वारितास्त्रेण निमित्तचपलेषुणा ।\nमहान्वनतरुर्विद्धो मृगं तत्र जिघांसता ॥","meaning":{"en":"With that hard-to-check missile, whose shaft wavered with his aim, he struck a great forest tree as he tried to kill the deer."}},{"n":5,"text":"स तीक्ष्णविषदिग्धेन शरेणातिबलात्कृतः ।\nउत्सृज्य फलपत्राणि पादपः शोषमागतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hit with great force by that arrow smeared with sharp poison, the tree shed its fruits and leaves and withered."}},{"n":6,"text":"तस्मिन्वृक्षे तथाभूते कोटरेषु चिरोषितः ।\nन जहाति शुको वासं तस्य भक्त्या वनस्पतेः ॥","meaning":{"en":"A parrot who had long lived in the hollows of that tree, now in such a state, would not leave his home, out of devotion to the lord of the forest."}},{"n":7,"text":"निष्प्रचारो निराहारो ग्लानः शिथिलवागपि ।\nकृतज्ञः सह वृक्षेण धर्मात्मा स व्यशुष्यत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Not moving about, not eating, wasting away, his voice faint, that grateful and righteous parrot dried up along with the tree."}},{"n":8,"text":"तमुदारं महासत्त्वमतिमानुषचेष्टितम् ।\nसमदुःखसुखं ज्ञात्वा विस्मितः पाकशासनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Knowing that noble, great-hearted bird, whose conduct was beyond the human and who shared the tree's pain and joy, Indra, the punisher of Paka, was astonished."}},{"n":9,"text":"ततश्चिन्तामुपगतः शक्रः कथमयं द्विजः ।\nतिर्यग्योनावसंभाव्यमानृशंस्यं समास्थितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Indra fell into thought: \"How has this bird, born in an animal womb, taken up compassion, which is hardly to be expected of such?\""}},{"n":10,"text":"अथ वा नात्र चित्रं हीत्यभवद्वासवस्य तु ।\nप्राणिनामिह सर्वेषां सर्वं सर्वत्र दृश्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Or \"perhaps it is no wonder,\" thought Indra, \"for in this world all things are seen in all creatures everywhere.\""}},{"n":11,"text":"ततो ब्राह्मणवेषेण मानुषं रूपमास्थितः ।\nअवतीर्य महीं शक्रस्तं पक्षिणमुवाच ह ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Indra took a human form in the guise of a brahmin, descended to earth, and spoke to the bird."}},{"n":12,"text":"शुक भोः पक्षिणां श्रेष्ठ दाक्षेयी सुप्रजास्त्वया ।\nपृच्छे त्वा शुष्कमेतं वै कस्मान्न त्यजसि द्रुमम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Parrot, best of birds, child of Dakshi's line, with good offspring, I ask you: why do you not leave this withered tree?\""}},{"n":13,"text":"अथ पृष्टः शुकः प्राह मूर्ध्ना समभिवाद्य तम् ।\nस्वागतं देवराजाय विज्ञातस्तपसा मया ॥","meaning":{"en":"Asked thus, the parrot bowed his head to him and said, \"Welcome, king of gods; I have recognized you by my austerity.\""}},{"n":14,"text":"ततो दशशताक्षेण साधु साध्विति भाषितम् ।\nअहो विज्ञानमित्येवं तपसा पूजितस्ततः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the thousand-eyed god said, \"Well done, well done! What insight!\" and so honored the parrot for his austerity."}},{"n":15,"text":"तमेवं शुभकर्माणं शुकं परमधार्मिकम् ।\nविजानन्नपि तां प्राप्तिं पप्रच्छ बलसूदनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Though he knew the reason, Indra, destroyer of Bala, asked that parrot of noble deeds and great righteousness:"}},{"n":16,"text":"निष्पत्रमफलं शुष्कमशरण्यं पतत्रिणाम् ।\nकिमर्थं सेवसे वृक्षं यदा महदिदं वनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"This tree is leafless, fruitless, withered, and no shelter for birds. Why do you serve it when this forest is so large?"}},{"n":17,"text":"अन्येऽपि बहवो वृक्षाः पत्रसंछन्नकोटराः ।\nशुभाः पर्याप्तसंचारा विद्यन्तेऽस्मिन्महावने ॥","meaning":{"en":"In this great forest there are many other trees whose hollows are covered with leaves, fine and with ample room to move."}},{"n":18,"text":"गतायुषमसामर्थ्यं क्षीणसारं हतश्रियम् ।\nविमृश्य प्रज्ञया धीर जहीमं ह्यस्थिरं द्रुमम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Reflect with your wisdom, steadfast one, and leave this unstable tree whose life is spent, which is powerless, drained of sap and robbed of splendor.\""}},{"n":19,"text":"तदुपश्रुत्य धर्मात्मा शुकः शक्रेण भाषितम् ।\nसुदीर्घमभिनिःश्वस्य दीनो वाक्यमुवाच ह ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing what Indra said, the righteous parrot sighed deeply and spoke sadly."}},{"n":20,"text":"अनतिक्रमणीयानि दैवतानि शचीपते ।\nयत्राभवस्तत्र भवस्तन्निबोध सुराधिप ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Husband of Shachi, the gods cannot be transgressed; chief of the gods, understand that where there was birth, there should be devotion."}},{"n":21,"text":"अस्मिन्नहं द्रुमे जातः साधुभिश्च गुणैर्युतः ।\nबालभावे च संगुप्तः शत्रुभिश्च न धर्षितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"I was born in this tree, endowed with good qualities, protected in my childhood, and never harmed by enemies."}},{"n":22,"text":"किमनुक्रोशवैफल्यमुत्पादयसि मेऽनघ ।\nआनृशंस्येऽनुरक्तस्य भक्तस्यानुगतस्य च ॥","meaning":{"en":"Blameless one, why do you make my compassion fruitless, when I am attached to compassion, devoted and loyal?"}},{"n":23,"text":"अनुक्रोशो हि साधूनां सुमहद्धर्मलक्षणम् ।\nअनुक्रोशश्च साधूनां सदा प्रीतिं प्रयच्छति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Compassion is the great mark of dharma among the good, and the compassion of the good always brings joy."}},{"n":24,"text":"त्वमेव दैवतैः सर्वैः पृच्छ्यसे धर्मसंशयान् ।\nअतस्त्वं देव देवानामाधिपत्ये प्रतिष्ठितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"You are asked by all the gods about doubts of dharma; that is why you are established as sovereign of the gods."}},{"n":25,"text":"नार्हसि त्वं सहस्राक्ष त्याजयित्वेह भक्तितः ।\nसमर्थमुपजीव्येमं त्यजेयं कथमद्य वै ॥","meaning":{"en":"You should not, thousand-eyed one, make me abandon my devotion here. Having lived by this tree when it was strong, how could I leave it today?\""}},{"n":26,"text":"तस्य वाक्येन सौम्येन हर्षितः पाकशासनः ।\nशुकं प्रोवाच धर्मज्ञमानृशंस्येन तोषितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Delighted by his gentle words and pleased with his compassion, Indra said to the parrot, who knew dharma:"}},{"n":27,"text":"वरं वृणीष्वेति तदा स च वव्रे वरं शुकः ।\nआनृशंस्यपरो नित्यं तस्य वृक्षस्य संभवम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Choose a boon.\" And the parrot, ever devoted to compassion, chose the revival of that tree."}},{"n":28,"text":"विदित्वा च दृढां शक्रस्तां शुके शीलसंपदम् ।\nप्रीतः क्षिप्रमथो वृक्षममृतेनावसिक्तवान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Knowing the parrot's firm excellence of character, Indra was pleased and quickly sprinkled the tree with nectar."}},{"n":29,"text":"ततः फलानि पत्राणि शाखाश्चापि मनोरमाः ।\nशुकस्य दृढभक्तित्वाच्छ्रीमत्त्वं चाप स द्रुमः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, through the parrot's firm devotion, the tree gained fruits, leaves, lovely branches and splendor."}},{"n":30,"text":"शुकश्च कर्मणा तेन आनृशंस्यकृतेन ह ।\nआयुषोऽन्ते महाराज प्राप शक्रसलोकताम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"And by that deed of compassion, O great king, the parrot at the end of his life attained Indra's world."}},{"n":31,"text":"एवमेव मनुष्येन्द्र भक्तिमन्तं समाश्रितः ।\nसर्वार्थसिद्धिं लभते शुकं प्राप्य यथा द्रुमः ॥","meaning":{"en":"In the same way, lord of men, one who relies on a devoted person gains success in every aim, as the tree did by getting the parrot."}}]}]}